  The finite-measure and Hilbert-space arguments are reorganized in ordinary
  mathematics. Quotienting by null vectors then completing is equivalent to
  the source's separated seminormed completion. The full-mesh lemma isolates
  uniqueness of complex limits from the larger <verbatim|Spec.Final> package.
  The final assembly specializes the blocking penalty to 1 and the initial
  mesh order to the identity; it preserves the same family and hierarchy in
  all four endpoint properties.

  <section|Literature and editorial decisions><label|literature-and-editorial-decisions>

  Scott Armstrong's source-cluster map at
  <verbatim|8f3c7ccaeabb17b0f928bc1a2e75328691de3032>, credited in the
  repository's <hlink|outline|../../outline.tm>, was used for navigation
  only. The parent read the live <hlink|#11 audit / PR
  #18|https://github.com/hairer/humanise-yang-mills/pull/18> and rechecked
  the meaning-determining source. Its files and existing literature task
  outputs were not edited.

  The parent inspected the original Osterwalder\USchrader 1975 paper,
  <em|Communications in Mathematical Physics> 42, 281\U305,
  <hlink|PDF|https://projecteuclid.org/journals/communications-in-mathematical-physics/volume-42/issue-3/Axioms-for-Euclidean-Greens-functions-II-with-an-Appendix-by/cmp/1103899050.pdf>,
  introduction and ŸIV.1, pp. 287\U288. The corrected sufficient theorem
  requires growth control in addition to the Euclidean axioms. The manuscript
  cites it only as a possible route with outstanding hypothesis checks. In
  particular <verbatim|Table.Capped> allows constants depending on each fixed
  label tuple and arity; it is not by itself a checked match for the paper's
  arity-growth condition. The reviewer could not independently retrieve the
  PDF and does not certify its application. No claim is made to have
  completed the separately owned literature task #6.

  The finite Wilson proofs use elementary matrix algebra, compactness and
  probability Haar invariance. The lattice drafter's Wilson-paper search did
  not obtain a verified substitute for any RG estimate. Source constructor
  names, bookkeeping, and undefined estimate norms have been removed from the
  mathematical narrative; their substantive unproved content remains in the
  evidence and obligations below.

